Here is a simple example of real-time email validation using plain JavaScript in a safe and sanitized format:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Email Validation Example</title>
  <style>
    .error {
      color: red;
      display: none;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <form>
    <label for="email">Email:</label>
    <input type="email" id="email" name="email" required>
    <div id="error-message" class="error">Please enter a valid email address.</div>
    <button type="submit">Submit</button>
  </form>

  <script>
    const emailInput = document.getElementById('email');
    const errorMessage = document.getElementById('error-message');

    emailInput.addEventListener('input', function() {
      const emailPattern = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/;
      if (emailPattern.test(emailInput.value)) {
        errorMessage.style.display = 'none';
      } else {
        errorMessage.style.display = 'block';
      }
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This example includes:
- An email input field with HTML5 validation attributes.
- A hidden error message that appears when the input does not match the email pattern.
- A JavaScript event listener that checks the input value in real-time and toggles the error message accordingly.

